Nope.

>I'm on a MicroVAX 3500 running ULTRIX-32 ver. 2.2 0 (VAX architecture)
>I'm running TinyMud ver. 1.5.3, but experienced similar problems with
>1.4.1 through 1.5.3.  The crash frequency has been about once every
>4 days on the average.  Does ANYONE have a clue?!?!?
Check the output of "netstat -m", make sure your not running out of
mbufs.  I've seen old talk do this but never tinymud.

If "netstat -m" shows more than "0 requests for memory denied" then you
have a problem.

If that isn't it, it could be just about anything else.  Best bet is to
dig through the crash data and try and find out what's going on.  It's
gotta be a bug in the OS or hardware (user programs should never be able
to crash the system) so you might should get support (dec or whoever)
to check it out.

Good luck,
